//! **Sakura Keep** — a Japanese castle town on a plateau over the void (DESIGN.md "Maps"; feature
//! `sakura`). PRIVATE USE: the floor plan follows Overwatch's Hanamura (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
//! "Maps"); the look, palette, props and name are ours. Replace the layout before any public release.
//!
//! The layout lives in [`layout`] (generated by `tools/maps/sakura_trace.py`: the playable outline,
//! terraces, stairs, buildings, trees, lanterns... in the reference image's pixel frame); this file
//! turns it into voxels. Flow (south → north-east):
//!
//! ```text
//!   spawn street (10 m) ─ steps ─ first-gate plaza (11.5) ─ gate steps ─ A district (13):
//!     A hall (14, tall, gallery) · west wing · courtyard · long arcade · middle street · north street
//!   middle street ─ bridge / SE lane ─ sakura garden (14.5): shrine + koi pond, temple hall
//!   garden ─ keep steps ─ castle base (17): keep hall (22 m tall, two balcony rings, painted panel)
//!     under a three-tier tenshu (top ≈ 57 m) · wings with walkable roofs · NW wing · north annex
//! ```
//!
//! - **Plateau over the void.** Everything stands on a 10–17 m plateau (bedrock at y = 0). A ring of
//!   town-house roofs lines the outline (walkable, with the drop to the void behind them); some edges
//!   are open (the ravine between the A district and the garden, the lower-garden cliff, the east
//!   plaza, the west street) with only a kerb. Falling past [`VOID_Y`] is a void KO; the sides are 24 m
//!   past the world, the top 40 m over it (star KO).
//! - **Destruction.** Houses, halls, roofs, trees and the ring break; the castle's stone base, the
//!   keep's pillars and the bedrock don't ([`pal::KEEP_CORE`], [`pal::PILLAR_CORE`]).
//! - **Movement.** Roof ridges are flat-topped walkways (bhop lines), eaves and sakura canopies are
//!   tether anchors, the keep hall is a 22 m swing room, and two hard-light surf lines run off the
//!   rooftops ([`ArenaInfo::surf_lines`]).
//! - **Light.** Warm afternoon sun; paper lanterns, shoji and sconces are emissive voxels (no point
//!   lights).

// Generator style: column loops index several per-column tables at once.
#![allow(
    clippy::needless_range_loop,
    clippy::too_many_arguments,
    clippy::type_complexity,
    clippy::manual_is_multiple_of,
    clippy::manual_range_contains
)]

